<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8960" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŏhortātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		cohortor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an exhorting</i>, <i>inciting;
				exhortation</i>, <i>encouragement</i> (rare, but
			in good prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">militum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep. Hann. 11, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legionis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 2, 25</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caesaris, Auct. B. Alex. 22: ducis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 14, 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">judicum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Clu. 50, 138</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incredibiliter me commovet tua cohortatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 16, 13</span></i>
			, C, 2; so <i><span class="en">id. Fam. 1, 7, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. de
				Or. 1, 47, 204</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">his cohortationibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 61, 262</span></i>
			.</div>
